---
import { Code } from "astro:components";

import ComponentPage from "../../../layouts/ComponentPage.astro";
import AvatarDemo from "../../../components/AvatarDemo";
import { codeTheme } from "../../../components/code-theme";

const fallbackExample = `<Avatar alt="Grace Hopper" size="sm" />
<Avatar alt="Grace Hopper" fallback="GMH" size="lg" />`;

const decorativeExample = `<p className="flex items-center gap-2">
  <Avatar src={user.photo} alt="" />
  {user.name}
</p>`;
---

<ComponentPage slug="avatar">
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    <code>alt</code> is required, so every avatar either has a name or is marked decorative.
  </Fragment>

  <AvatarDemo slot="demo" client:visible />

  <Fragment slot="usage">
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <li>
        <strong>Name it with alt.</strong> Use the person's name, such as "Ada Lovelace", not
        "avatar" or "profile picture".
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Initials fallback.</strong> With no <code>src</code>, or when the image fails to
        load, the avatar shows initials taken from <code>alt</code> (or <code>fallback</code>). The
        fallback has <code>role="img"</code> with <code>alt</code> as its name, and the initials are
        <code>aria-hidden</code>, so screen readers hear "Ada Lovelace, image", not "A L".
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sizes.</strong> <code>sm</code> (32px), <code>default</code> (40px) and
        <code>lg</code> (48px). The initials use the muted colors; in forced-colors mode a border
        keeps the circle visible.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="examples">
    <h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Sizes and a custom fallback</h3>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm [&_pre]:p-4">
      <Code code={fallbackExample} lang="tsx" theme={codeTheme} />
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-8 font-display text-lg">Decorative avatars</h3>
    <p class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
      When the name is already next to the avatar, pass <code>alt=""</code>. The image, or its
      fallback, is then hidden from screen readers, so the name is not read twice:
    </p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm [&_pre]:p-4">
      <Code code={decorativeExample} lang="tsx" theme={codeTheme} />
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <p slot="install-notes" class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
    It creates <code>components/ui/avatar.tsx</code>, the same path as shadcn's Avatar, but as one
    component: <code>src</code>, <code>alt</code> and <code>fallback</code> are props instead of
    <code>AvatarImage</code> and <code>AvatarFallback</code> parts. It needs
    <code>class-variance-authority</code> and your <code>cn()</code> helper; if your
    <code>lib/utils.ts</code> differs from the current shadcn version, the CLI asks before replacing
    it, and answering no is safe.
  </p>
</ComponentPage>
